From: Werner Stein <werner.stein@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:21:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(manual): explain agent push doctor diagnostics

Explain the explicit inspection flags and warning semantics so operators
can act on missing forge evidence without treating a diagnostic result as
permission to run or a waiver of mandatory enforcement.

Refs: #538
Co-Authored-By: Codex gpt-6.1-sol <noreply@openai.com>
---
 .../content/docs/manual/run-the-supervisor.md | 32 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/content/docs/manual/run-the-supervisor.md b/docs/content/docs/manual/run-the-supervisor.md
index a135ada0..4bb45d88 100644
--- a/docs/content/docs/manual/run-the-supervisor.md
+++ b/docs/content/docs/manual/run-the-supervisor.md
@@ -27,6 +27,38 @@ and `whr doctor --user <your-account>`. The doctor warns, and does not fail, whe
 from outside an administrator-owned prefix. See the [source installation](install-upgrade-release.md)
 for the alpha policy and the service behavior.
 
+For an installation using agent topic push, request its read-only forge diagnostic:
+
+```text
+whr doctor --agent-topic-push --agent-app-id <agent-app-id>
+```
+
+`--agent-topic-push` requests inspection; it does not enable pushes. Automatic
+activation from runtime configuration is pending a configuration contract. The
+optional `--agent-app-id` identifies the agent's GitHub App, independently of the
+supervisor App that reads the evidence. Omit it when that identity is unknown;
+the check then reports `not_verified`. It does not establish a non-App agent's
+identity or token permissions.
+
+The `agent-push-ruleset` check reads each configured repository's default and
+integration branches (including the default `develop` for the integration
+workflow). It reports observed requirements for a pull request and an approving
+review, plus the agent App's bypass coverage. Missing policy, an agent bypass,
+or enforcement that remains unconfirmed produces `warn`; an unreachable forge,
+unavailable identity or incomplete visibility produces `not_verified`. Neither
+status causes a failing exit by itself. The report names repository rules settings
+links for human follow-up and changes no forge settings. To omit this inspection
+for one report, use `--skip agent-push-ruleset` with `--agent-topic-push`.
+
+Observed branch rules do not prove that a reviewer is human. Outside-topic branch
+restrictions, tag restrictions and release/deployment denial remain explicitly
+`not_verified`; this diagnostic does not measure them. Live visibility and denial
+with the actual agent identity remain {{< status unverified >}} (#230, #542 and
+#27). A warning, a `not_verified` result, or a skipped check does not waive the
+mandatory [R-30 forge controls](../requirements.md), admit a runtime, authorize
+agent merge/tag/release/deploy, or start or resume a run. Existing admission
+controls and [D57 human initiation](../design/security.md) still apply.
+
